  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They never trailed, and Baltimore couldn't mount anything close.",
    "what_this_means": "Warren's 5.2 innings of four-hit ball stabilized a game that could have gotten messy early. The bullpen. Cruz for 1.1 scoreless, Hill picking up the hold, Bednar closing clean. Asked little of the lineup and received what it needed. But the real separation came in the third inning. Five runs on a foundation Goldschmidt built: a two-run homer that turned early control into early cushion. Judge added a two-hit night. Nine strikeouts and seven hits across the rest of the roster tells you how the burden was divided. This team doesn't win many games on margin. But they win them when pitching and one cold-contact bat align at exactly the right moment. Early leads matter less than leads that hold, and this one did.",
    "what_to_watch": "Kyle Bradish takes the mound tonight for Baltimore with a 4.83 ERA that the Yankees lineup should recognize immediately as an opening.",
